cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BimodalLogic: A Lean 4 Formalization of the Bimodal Logic TM"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it formalizes."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brast-McKie
    given-names: Benjamin
    email: benjamin@logos-labs.ai
repository-code: "https://github.com/benbrastmckie/BimodalLogic"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of TM, the bimodal logic of Tense and Modality, which combines S5
  modal operators with the Since/Until linear tense operators over task semantics. The
  development carries machine-checked soundness, weak completeness and finite-context
  consequence completeness at all four frame classes, strong completeness and compactness at
  two of them, machine-checked refutations of strong completeness at the other two, and a
  one-directional tableau decision procedure. Every headline result's axiom set is asserted on
  every build; the per-theorem ledger is docs/theorem-index.md.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - modal logic
  - temporal logic
  - bimodal logic
  - completeness
  - formalized mathematics
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The Construction of Possible Worlds"
    authors:
      - family-names: Brast-McKie
        given-names: Benjamin
    journal: "Journal of Philosophical Logic"
    publisher:
      name: Springer
    year: 2026
    notes: "Forthcoming. The paper this repository formalizes."
    url: "https://benbrastmckie.com/publications/possible_worlds.pdf"
